            "subworkflow": {
                "a_galaxy_workflow": "true",
                "annotation": "",
                "comments": [],
                "creator": [
                    {
                        "class": "Person",
                        "identifier": "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-0059-1887",
                        "name": "Niklas Mayle"
                    }
                ],
                "format-version": "0.1",
                "license": "MIT",
                "name": "Split BAM by Path",
                "readme": "## What This Workflow Does\n\nThis workflow takes two input files:\n* **BAM file:** The main aligned sequence dataset.\n* **Path List File:** A text file containing target paths, or contigs (one per line).\n\n### Process\n1. **Splits the path list:** Breaks the input list into individual single-line text files.\n2. **Filters the BAM:** Parses the path/contig from each text file and extracts the matching reads from the main BAM file.\n3. **Generates individual BAMs:** Creates a collection of smaller, contig-specific BAM files.\n\nThis enables downstream tools to analyze individual contigs concurrently, potentially speeding up execution times.",
                "report": {
                    "markdown": "\n# Workflow Execution Report\n\n## Workflow Inputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_inputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow Outputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_outputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow\n```galaxy\nworkflow_display()\n```\n"
                },
